<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Save-Path Invariants — IslandAdaptor Outbound

Path K / F-arc: outbound hygiene for sustained live wiki authoring.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/problem>>

!! Problem Space

`IslandAdaptor.saveTiddler` acts as the boundary where TW5 wiki edits cross
into the Automerge store. Without hygiene here, sustained editing produces:

* ''Write amplification'' — every keystroke fires a store write + CRDT patch +
  disk-projector file write. At 5 keystrokes/sec over a 10-minute session:
  3 000 store writes, 3 000 disk writes, all for the same tiddler.
* ''Noisy projection state'' — parse-warning tiddlers, `$:/state/*` fragments,
  and boot-splash signals accumulate in the wiki. Some carry `lar:` URIs and
  could bleed into the store without guards.
* ''Draft routing confusion'' — draft tiddlers from TW5 editing UX
  should reach the per-wiki draft bag, not get silently dropped.

The law this path enacts stands at `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/outbound-bridge#/the-shore-law`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/invariants>>

!! Invariants

!!! SP-1 — The Pacing Gate

`saveTiddler` and `deleteTiddler` MUST mark their TITLE in one per-title gate (`HandGate`,
`packages/lararium-tw5/src/hand-gate.ts`): a trailing window of ''400 ms'' under a non-resetting cap
of ''2 s''.

* A later mark of the same title restarts the trailing window and leaves the cap running, so
  continuous typing reaches the store within the cap.
* What leaves at the flush MUST equal the title's state in the wiki at that flush, never the value
  a mark carried. A state equal to the landed value with nothing sent since leaves nothing. One
  exception: a direct caller that hands in a tiddler the wiki does not hold rides pinned, and its
  value stands in for the wiki's.
* The returned promise settles at flush time, not at call time; every caller that marked the title
  settles with that flush. Callers MUST tolerate asynchronous settlement.
* A discrete act (a draft's save, rename or cancel) MUST take its titles out of the gate and leave
  in the dispatch turn, with no wait.
* `stop()` MUST flush every marked title and MUST NOT drop a pending write.
* The timers pace and decide nothing; a refused write arms no timer.

Rationale: human keystroke rate typically runs 3–8 chars/sec. A 400 ms window
coalesces a full word or short phrase into a single store write. Stays below
perceived lag threshold (< 1 s).

!!! SP-2 — Ephemeral Truncation

The VOLATILE VM PLANE (`lar:///lararium.local.vm/…`, `VOLATILE_VM_PREFIX` in
`packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts`) MUST NOT reach the Automerge store.
`saveTiddler` and `deleteTiddler` refuse it by `isVolatileVmUri`, ahead of the
cascade, so no cascade edit can lift the refusal (`island-adaptor.ts`).

Once the shore turns resident, every OTHER title a wiki write touches reaches the outbound
bridge, whichever door wrote it: the bridge skips foam, sends a standing hand to `saveTiddler` and a gone hand
to `deleteTiddler`, and the cascade's
`[prefix[lar:]]` rule routes a `lar:` title to `current-wiki-bag`. So wiki
scratch that must stay off the store lives under the volatile plane; a scratch
title spelled anywhere else (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/state/…`, a parse-warning title)
persists like any authored tiddler. The alert rail (`$:/temp/lares/alert/…`) never
persists either (`neverPersists`).

!!! SP-3 — Draft Routing

Draft tiddlers from TW5 editing UX (a `draft.of` field standing) MUST route to the wiki's per-wiki
draft slot (`wikis/{slug}/draft`, a CRDT layer that follows the operator's fleet)
and MUST NOT be silently dropped. The in-wiki bag-paths cascade carries the rule
(`[is[draft]then{…/current-wiki-draft}]`), read against TW5's `draft.of` FIELD,
never the title; the matching delete routes by the bag the draft last wrote to or
landed from, since the field has gone by then, and a draft's deletion inside a save, rename or
cancel leaves with that act. No guard in `saveTiddler` withholds a
draft. The cascade names its withholdings (`$:/core`, `$:/library/sjcl.js`) and
ends in a catch-all — a title no rule reaches lands at the write layer and says
so (wiki-layer-ontology#/totality-law). The measured routing table rides
recipe-layer-model#/as-routed.

!!! SP-4 — Ceremony Routing

No field on a saved tiddler names its destination bag: `draft.of` selects the draft route, and a
draft's store-only base fields record its target's base and route nothing. Residency rides the ENVELOPE: the store fires
each change with its own bag, the nalu stamps `$origin-bag` on the wiki side for
the projector, and the outbound save strips that stamp before the write. `bag`
stays the author's own field and never routes. A ceremony that targets one
specific bag (MOVE, promotion, `meme put --bag`) carries the bag on the write
OPTION (`store.put(record, origin, { bag })`) — never on the record — and a
bag with no writable layer refuses loud rather than falling through to the
default writable (wiki-layer-ontology#/write-law).

Live TW5 edits route by the cascade and the composition's layer order: `_saveBag(title)` names the layer, at or above the working layer, and the write carries it as the `{ bag }` option.

!!! SP-5 — Single Parser Law

All inbound meme text passes through `splitBodyTiddler()` (ONE parser,
FOUR call sites law). `_writeMeme` upholds this; do not add a second parse
site.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/debounce-design>>

!! Gate Design

```
saveTiddler(tiddler): Promise<void>
  → refuse a title that never persists (the volatile VM plane · the alert rail)
  → teach the draft book when the tiddler carries draft.of
  → remember the hand's base (the ledger's bag + heads) at the first mark
  → gate.mark(title, flush)        trailing 400 ms · cap 2 s

_flushHand(title)
  → wait for any in-flight write of the title
  → read the title's state in the wiki
  → settled (equal to the landed value, or to the value already sent)? leave nothing
  → _saveBag(title) · _basePlan(title, bag)      a refused route stays owed
  → _writeMeme(title, fields, origin, bag, base) → store.writeFamily
  → settle every waiter of the mark on resolve/reject
```

State the gate holds per marked title (`hand-gate.ts`):

| Field | Lifecycle |
|---|---|
| `trailing` | the resetting timer; cleared at flush or when a discrete act consumes the title |
| `cap` | the non-resetting timer armed at the first mark; cleared the same way |
| `flush` | the latest flush closure for the title |
| `waiters` | every caller's resolve/reject pair, settled together |

On `stop()`: the adaptor awaits discrete acts in flight, stops the landing queue, flushes every
marked title, and unsubscribes from the projection bus. A write that fails at teardown reports its
title on the console.

<<~/ahu>>

